This program models the slab as a graph where each node is a cell with black or white pixels. Each time a cell with a color changes (is changed from white to black or from black to white), these changes must first update any adjacent cells. Thus, the program should determine the minimal number of cells that should change by traversing the entire graph appearing after a change occurs (each cell showing a color is split, and other cells above or beside it must change too). This would require all the colours in the rows spanning over into neighboring lines unless such adjacent line regions have similar colours.

